      "finding": "Two fixture std::println macros failed the repository diagnostic-writer lint; replaced with note! and qualified full-workspace Clippy.",
      "fixed_at": "e58e0597483b0c53aa09caa866709ddb7fe14aab"
    },
    {
      "finding": "Prior Python CI alarm failure discarded its HTTP body. Diagnostic change retains status/body and does not retry HTTP 500 or weaken the assertion. A focused passing replay does not close that CI finding.",
      "related_ci": "https://github.com/crabbuild/cellar/actions/runs/39723205982/job/119641154633"
    },
    {
      "finding": "A development broad run also hit the S3 seed setup Overloaded refusal. The frozen final CLI matrix passed, while a later targeted probe reproduced and repaired the setup race in the separate receipt-maintenance record. A passing replay alone is not the repair."
    }
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Raft daemons pin the initial compiled deployment until process restart; live Raft definition rebinding is not implemented.",
    "Remote peers/query origins/inspection origins require a real Fleet bucket so the daemon obtains shared peer authentication; independently injecting an object store is insufficient.",
    "Receipt maintenance, remaining management operations and verified fenced disaster restore are separate components.",
    "Prior transfer, concurrent fallback and effect callback-count findings remain open. Additional 3.14t CI reports contain nonmember reads and Fleet event recovery/drain failures; this serial native matrix does not close those findings.",
